<title>UK: General Accident weak as sellers return.</title>
<headline>General Accident weak as sellers return.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK insurance company General Accident Plc fell on Wednesday after a turnaround in the U.S. bond market overnight encouraged selling in the stock.</p>
<p>The shares were off 24-1/2p to 765-1/2p by 1009 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;General Accident is heavily exposed to the U.S. bond market,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>&quot;The share price is a reflection of the sharp turnaround in bonds yesterday, there were some sellers around before that but this has just added fuel to the fire,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
